      "type": "OWNER_LOCK",
      "status": "OWNER_LOCK",
      "text": "Na'aseh is Qal imperfect 1cp, expressing Let Us make in direct divine speech. It is NOT wayyiqtol and must never be rendered shape/shaped."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.26",
      "lemma": "120",
      "type": "HUMANITY_CONTEXT",
      "status": "RESEARCH_ONLY",
      "text": "Adam here can refer to the human/humankind. Capitalized Man is a researched literal rendering, not by itself a determination that a personal name is used."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.26",
      "lemma": "6754",
      "type": "IMAGE",
      "status": "RESEARCH_ONLY",
      "text": "Tselem is image, with a 1cp pronominal suffix in betsalmenu (Our image). The grammatical plural should be retained without claiming the plural alone proves a particular Trinity interpretation."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.26",
      "lemma": "1823",
      "type": "LIKENESS",
      "status": "RESEARCH_ONLY",
      "text": "Demut is a distinct lexeme meaning likeness, with 1cp suffix. Image and likeness are not automatically interchangeable Hebrew homonyms."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.26",
      "lemma": "6213 a",
      "type": "CHRISTOLOGICAL_CANONICAL_PARALLEL",
      "status": "RESEARCH_ONLY",
      "text": "John 1:1–3 and Colossians 1:15–17 are Christian canonical parallels for divine agency and image. This is exegetical Christology, not a source-based claim that asah's lexical meaning is Christ."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.27",
      "lemma": "1254 a",
      "type": "OWNER_LOCK",
      "status": "OWNER_LOCK",
      "text": "The first bara is wayyiqtol while the two later bara forms are Qal qatal 3ms. All three follow the OLT family shape/shaped, but morphological classifications differ."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.27",
      "lemma": "853",
      "type": "OBJECT_PRONOUN",
      "status": "SOURCE_MORPHOLOGY_UNREVIEWED",
      "text": "Et as zero-surface accusative marker differs from oto = him (Sp3ms) and otam = them (Sp3mp). Their pronominal suffixes must be expressed."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.28",
      "lemma": "3533",
      "type": "IMPERATIVE_FEMININE_SUFFIX",
      "status": "SOURCE_MORPHOLOGY_UNREVIEWED",
      "text": "Vekivshuha is Qal imperative second masculine plural with a 3fs object suffix, referring to Earth; OLT proposal and subdue her is grammar-visible, never it."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.28",
      "lemma": "7287 a",
      "type": "GOVERNANCE_VERB",
      "status": "SOURCE_MORPHOLOGY_UNREVIEWED",
      "text": "The imperative and rule in verse 28 differs from the preceding jussive and let them rule in 1:26."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.29",
      "lemma": "5414",
      "type": "QATAL_NOT_WAYYIQTOL",
      "status": "SOURCE_MORPHOLOGY_UNREVIEWED",
      "text": "Nattati is Qal perfect 1cs, proposed I gave, not a source-wayyiqtol and not mechanically translated via the narrative past policy."
    },
    {
      "reference": "Gen.1.29",
      "lemma": "1961",
      "type": "IMPERFECT",
      "status": "SOURCE_MORPHOLOGY_UNREVIEWED",
      "text": "Yihyeh is Qal imperfect 3ms. The proposal [he] shall be makes a supplied referential English pronoun visible, rather than introducing the forbidden neutral it."
